From: Ian Petersen <ispeters@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] DIAGNOSTIC: env-gated reserve + instrumentation on UnsubstitutedConstraintSatisfactionCache

NOT FOR UPSTREAM. Experimental knockout probe for the nondeterministic
crash tracked at llvm/llvm-project#191361.

Supersedes the previous two versions of this patch.

  * The =1 arm reserves a single entry (DenseMap's 64-bucket floor) and
    lets the map grow normally. This is deliberate and KEPT: it exercises
    the same getenv/strtoul/reserve() path at a magnitude too small to
    suppress anything, which isolates any observed effect to the reserve
    size rather than to the presence of the hook. An earlier revision of
    this patch documented =1 as selecting the default; that comment was
    wrong (only 0 or an unparseable value does), and is now fixed.

  * Reports the cache's bucket footprint at construction and its peak
    entry count plus footprint at end-of-TU, so the intervention is
    observable rather than assumed. Equal "buckets=" figures mean
    DenseMap::grow() never fired, i.e. the rehash-under-recursion
    mechanism really was removed.

    The end-of-TU report deliberately does NOT live in ~Sema(): the
    driver passes -disable-free to cc1 by default, so Sema is never
    destroyed in a normal compile and a destructor hook never runs. An
    earlier revision made that mistake and silently produced no output.

Both reports are gated on the env var and go to stderr, so rate-counting
loops that discard stderr are unaffected. A crashing run aborts before
end-of-TU, so take peak size from a successful run.

Arms:
  unset  -> stock behaviour (control)
  =1     -> reserve 1 entry (no-op treatment; specificity control)
  =N     -> reserve N entries
  =0     -> reserve 1<<17 entries (~88 MB of buckets; a large heap
            perturbation in its own right, hence the dose-response sweep)

NOTE: paths in this diff are relative to the `clang/` subdirectory of
the llvm-project monorepo, to match this repo's clang derivation's
sourceRoot (clang-src-.../clang).
---
diff --git a/lib/Sema/Sema.cpp b/lib/Sema/Sema.cpp
index 5a7dfb1..b02d581 100644
--- a/lib/Sema/Sema.cpp
+++ b/lib/Sema/Sema.cpp
@@ -76,6 +76,8 @@
 #include "llvm/ADT/SetVector.h"
 #include "llvm/ADT/SmallPtrSet.h"
 #include "llvm/Support/TimeProfiler.h"
+#include "llvm/Support/raw_ostream.h"
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <optional>
 
 using namespace clang;
@@ -358,6 +360,42 @@ Sema::Sema(Preprocessor &pp, ASTContext &ctxt, ASTConsumer &consumer,
   SemaPPCallbackHandler->set(*this);
 
   CurFPFeatures.setFPEvalMethod(PP.getCurrentFPEvalMethod());
+
+  // DIAGNOSTIC HOOK (downstream patch, not for upstream).
+  //
+  // Pre-size UnsubstitutedConstraintSatisfactionCache so that DenseMap::grow()
+  // never runs after this point. A rehash from inside a nested
+  // ConstraintSatisfactionChecker::Evaluate() frees the old bucket array while
+  // outer Evaluate frames are still running; the freed range is later reused
+  // for ASTContext bump-allocator slabs.
+  //
+  // Gated on an env var so every arm shares one binary. NOTE the value
+  // semantics, which are what make the specificity control possible:
+  //
+  //   unset                             -> stock behaviour (control)
+  //   CLANG_CONSTRAINT_CACHE_RESERVE=1  -> reserve *one* entry: takes the same
+  //                                        branch and calls reserve(), but the
+  //                                        map grows normally afterwards, so
+  //                                        this is a no-op treatment arm
+  //   CLANG_CONSTRAINT_CACHE_RESERVE=N  -> reserve N entries
+  //   CLANG_CONSTRAINT_CACHE_RESERVE=0  -> reserve 1<<17 entries (the default;
+  //                                        0 and unparseable values land here)
+  //
+  // Reports go to stderr only when the variable is set, so the rate-counting
+  // loops (which discard stderr) are unaffected. Compare this "buckets="
+  // figure with the one reported at end-of-TU: if they are equal, grow()
+  // never fired and the rehash mechanism really was removed.
+  if (const char *Env = std::getenv("CLANG_CONSTRAINT_CACHE_RESERVE")) {
+    unsigned long Entries = std::strtoul(Env, nullptr, 10);
+    if (Entries == 0)
+      Entries = 1ul << 17;
+    UnsubstitutedConstraintSatisfactionCache.reserve(
+        static_cast<unsigned>(Entries));
+    llvm::errs() << "[constraint-cache] reserved " << Entries
+                 << " entries; buckets="
+                 << UnsubstitutedConstraintSatisfactionCache.getMemorySize()
+                 << " bytes\n";
+  }
 }
 
 // Anchor Sema's type info to this TU.
@@ -1718,6 +1756,23 @@ void Sema::ActOnEndOfTranslationUnit() {
     TUScope = nullptr;
 
   checkExposure(Context.getTranslationUnitDecl());
+
+  // DIAGNOSTIC HOOK (downstream patch, not for upstream). See the matching
+  // block in Sema's constructor.
+  //
+  // This deliberately lives here rather than in ~Sema(): the driver passes
+  // -disable-free to cc1 by default, so Sema is never destroyed in a normal
+  // compile and a destructor hook never fires. End-of-TU runs on every
+  // successful compile.
+  //
+  // "peak size" is the entry count to size a dose-response sweep around; an
+  // unchanged "buckets=" figure (vs. the constructor's) proves no rehash.
+  if (std::getenv("CLANG_CONSTRAINT_CACHE_RESERVE"))
+    llvm::errs() << "[constraint-cache] peak size="
+                 << UnsubstitutedConstraintSatisfactionCache.size()
+                 << "; buckets="
+                 << UnsubstitutedConstraintSatisfactionCache.getMemorySize()
+                 << " bytes\n";
 }
 
 
